CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*pair)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct fsl_asrc_pair)...)
#612: FILE: sound/soc/fsl/fsl_asrc_dma.c:314:
+	pair = kzalloc(sizeof(struct fsl_asrc_pair) + PAIR_PRIVAT_SIZE, GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

